    dict(key='14-act-4-figure', kind='figure', title='How the TCP checksum is made',
         body='checksum_steps',
         narration='Fourth demo: how a checksum is made, for the last SYN, as it was sent. [[slnc 600]] Step one. [[slnc 300]] Split the bytes into sixteen bit words. [[slnc 300]] First a pseudo header: the two addresses, the protocol number six for T C P, and the length, twenty. [[slnc 300]] Then the T C P header, with its checksum field set to zero. [[slnc 600]] Step two. [[slnc 300]] Add all sixteen words: three eight f two d. [[slnc 300]] Five hex digits, one too many. [[slnc 500]] Step three. [[slnc 300]] Fold the extra digit back in: eight f two d, plus three, is eight f three zero. [[slnc 500]] Step four. [[slnc 300]] Flip every bit: seven zero c f. [[slnc 300]] That is the checksum. [[slnc 300]] The receiver does the same sum to check it.'),
    dict(key='15-act-4', kind='console', title='Act Four — How a checksum is made, step by step',
         body='FOUR. How a checksum is made, step by step.\n  the packet: the SYN from 100.64.0.99, as it was sent\n  STEP 1. SPLIT INTO 16-BIT WORDS (checksum field 0000):\n    pseudo-header  6440 0063 cb00 710a 0006 0014\n    TCP header     9ca3 01bb 0000 0007 0000 0000\n                   5002 ffff 0000 0000\n  STEP 2. ADD THEM UP:\n    sum            38f2d\n  STEP 3. FOLD THE CARRY BACK IN:\n    8f2d + 3 = 8f30\n  STEP 4. FLIP EVERY BIT:\n    checksum       70cf\n  the checksum the packet carries: 70cf, the same: true',
         narration='Here are the same four steps, printed by the program. [[slnc 400]] The words. [[slnc 200]] The sum. [[slnc 200]] The fold. [[slnc 200]] And the flipped result, seven zero c f. [[slnc 400]] The last line compares it with the checksum the packet carries. [[slnc 300]] The same.'),
